<% sweep = Lab::SWEEPS.fetch("meta_stack") %>
<% seeds = sweep.fetch(:seeds) %>
<% epochs = number_with_delimiter sweep.fetch(:epochs), delimiter: " " %>
<% tape = Lab::MetaStackReading::META_BUNDLE %>
<% constants = Lab::MetaStackReading %>
<% repo_url = "https://github.com/hanscanonico/life_simulator/blob/main" %>
<% record_url = "#{repo_url}/docs/design_record.md" %>
<% studies_url = "#{repo_url}/docs/studies" %>
<% readings_url = "#{repo_url}/docs/readings/meta-stack" %>

<h2>Question</h2>
<p>
  <%= link_to "Given a NAND", finding_path("paid-logic-climbs-only-read-once-tasks") %>, paid
  replicators climbed every logic rung that reads its inputs once and stopped below XOR and EQU,
  the two that need an input twice. The
  <%= link_to "design study", "#{studies_url}/meta-stack.md" %> behind this sweep read the stall
  as <strong>fan-out in a two-head machine whose NAND writes in place</strong>: a value used
  twice needs a stored copy and re-aligned heads, and in a tape that must also copy itself only
  the copy loop supplies them. Meta-stack, the variant of the Metabolism substrate in DESIGN
  §1.4, moves the computing off the copier and changes what the NAND writes. <strong>On a tape
  the soup never runs, read with a NAND that keeps its operands, does a soup assemble XOR and
  EQU from paid parts?</strong>
</p>

<h2>Method</h2>
<p>
  The parents and seeds are the Logic sweep's: the emerged worlds the
  <%= link_to "from-emerged sweep", experiment_path("from-emerged") %> continued, each run
  another <%= epochs %> epochs, seeds <%= seeds.first %>–<%= seeds.last %>, under Logic's
  economy and paid ladder. Every child carries a second, <%= tape.fetch("meta_len") %>-byte
  <strong>metabolism tape</strong>, seeded from its cell's own tape. The soup never executes
  it; the logic assay reads it, and the world hands it on with each copy, mutating it at
  <%= tape.fetch("meta_rate") %> a byte. Three arms:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>meta-stack</strong>: every rung paid, the tape read with the stack NAND, which
    writes its result one cell to the left, moves its head there and leaves its operands
    intact.</li>
  <li><strong>meta-stack-deep-only</strong>: the same with only XOR and EQU paid, Lenski's
    control. It separates "the deep rungs are built on paid parts" from "the deep rungs are
    directly reachable".</li>
  <li><strong>meta-inplace</strong>: the tape read with Logic's NAND, which writes in place, the
    control on the NAND's semantics.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Each child is paired with the child of the same parent and seed in another arm. Two arms come
  from the <%= link_to "Logic sweep", experiment_path("logic") %>, no new run needed:
  <strong>logic-none</strong>, its unpaid child, and <strong>logic-full</strong>, its paid child
  computing on the copied tape itself.
</p>
<p>
  The reading is <strong>pre-registered</strong>, with every number fixed before a child was
  seeded: <%= link_to "docs/design_record.md", record_url %>, 2026-10-02, "Meta-stack: does a
  soup assemble the deep rungs from paid parts on a metabolism tape read with a stack NAND?",
  DESIGN §1.3 item 17. The rules are Logic's: a settling window of
  <%= number_with_delimiter constants::SETTLING_WINDOW, delimiter: " " %> epochs, last-decile
  medians, and no pair with an extinct child in a test. There are six one-sided sign tests at
  p &lt; <%= constants::SIGN_TEST_LEVEL %>:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>H-deep-Ms</strong>, the rung-4 question (meta-stack against logic-none):
    <span class="mono">logic_capability_deep</span>, the number of XOR and EQU held by a tenth
    of the world.
  </li>
  <li><strong>H-stones-Ms</strong> (meta-stack against meta-stack-deep-only): the same count.</li>
  <li><strong>H-stack</strong> (meta-stack against meta-inplace): the same count. Does the
    NAND's semantics decide it?</li>
  <li><strong>H-deep-M</strong> (meta-inplace against logic-none): the same count, the tape
    under the in-place NAND.</li>
  <li><strong>H-decouple</strong> (meta-inplace against logic-full): the same count, the tape
    against the copied tape under the same NAND.</li>
  <li><strong>H-capability-M</strong> (meta-stack against logic-none):
    <span class="mono">logic_capability</span>, every rung from ECHO to EQU.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Each test is also read with the extinct pairs kept and without the four parents the design
  study piloted (runs <%= constants::PILOT_PARENTS.to_sentence %>). Those two re-readings
  decide no outcome. A shown test lists any one or two parents whose pairs it cannot do
  without. The entry also locks three measurements made after the sweep on each deep child's
  stored worlds: a substitution distance, heritability by planting, and the circuit behind
  the deep solver.
</p>

<% reading = @show.meta_stack %>
<h2>Result</h2>
<% if reading&.any? %>
  <p>
    <% reading.tests.each do |test| %>
      <span class="badge <%= test.badge_class %>"><%= test.hypothesis %> <%= test.outcome_label %></span>
    <% end %>
    <% if reading.assembled? %>
      <strong>With a stack NAND on a metabolism tape, paid parts assembled the logic rungs that
      need an input twice.</strong>
    <% else %>
      <strong>The deep rungs did not read as assembled from paid parts: see the tests
      below.</strong>
    <% end %>
    <% if reading.interim? %>
      Not every child of this sweep and of the Logic sweep has finished, so this reading is
      interim.
    <% end %>
  </p>
  <ul id="meta-stack-finding-tests">
    <% reading.tests.each do |test| %>
      <% comparison = test.comparison %>
      <% leaning = reading.leaning(test) %>
      <% treatment = test.treatment.name %>
      <% control = test.control.name %>
      <li class="mb-3">
        <strong><%= test.hypothesis %></strong>, <%= treatment %> against <%= control %>:
        <%= comparison.favouring %> pairs favour <%= treatment %>, <%= comparison.against %>
        <%= control %> and <%= comparison.ties %> tie, of <%= comparison.measured_count %>
        measured<% if comparison.p_value %>, p = <%= p_value_text(comparison.p_value) %><% end %>,
        <span class="badge <%= test.badge_class %>"><%= test.outcome_label %></span>.
        <% if reading.unanimous?(test) %>
          Every pair of all <%= reading.parent_count %> parents favours <%= treatment %>.
        <% else %>
          By parent, <%= leaning.treated %> lean to <%= treatment %>, <%= leaning.tied %> tie
          throughout and <%= leaning.control %> lean to <%= control %>.
        <% end %>
        <% [["With the extinct pairs kept", reading.kept(test.hypothesis)],
            ["Without the piloted parents", reading.unpiloted(test.hypothesis)]].each do |label, sensitivity| %>
          <%= label %>: <%= sensitivity.comparison.favouring %> to
          <%= sensitivity.comparison.against %> with <%= sensitivity.comparison.ties %> ties<% if sensitivity.comparison.p_value %>,
          p = <%= p_value_text(sensitivity.comparison.p_value) %><% end %>,
          <span class="badge <%= sensitivity.badge_class %>"><%= sensitivity.outcome_label %></span>.
        <% end %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <% if reading.shown_tests.any? %>
    <p id="meta-stack-finding-leave-out">
      <% if reading.carried_tests.empty? %>
        No one or two parents carry a shown test: whichever one or two are left out, the rest
        still read p &lt; <%= constants::SIGN_TEST_LEVEL %>.
      <% else %>
        <% reading.carried_tests.each do |test| %>
          <%= test.hypothesis %> rests on parents
          <%= test.comparison.carried_by.map { |parents| parents.map { |id| "run #{id}" }.join(" and ") }.to_sentence(two_words_connector: " or ", last_word_connector: ", or ") %>.
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      <% reading.carried_sensitivities.each do |test| %>
        Re-read as <%= test.hypothesis %>, it rests on parents
        <%= test.comparison.carried_by.map { |parents| parents.map { |id| "run #{id}" }.join(" and ") }.to_sentence(two_words_connector: " or ", last_word_connector: ", or ") %>:
        without their pairs it falls to p ≥ <%= constants::SIGN_TEST_LEVEL %>.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
  <% deep = reading.deep_children %>
  <p id="meta-stack-finding-deep">
    <%= pluralize(deep.size, "meta-stack child", plural: "meta-stack children") %> of
    <%= reading.stack_arm.children.size %>, from <%= pluralize(reading.deep_parent_count, "parent") %>,
    held XOR or EQU at a tenth of the world for <%= constants::PERSISTENCE_RUN %> samples
    running. Every other arm reached a deep rung in
    <%= reading.arms.reject { |arm| arm == reading.stack_arm }.map { |arm| "#{reading.deep_count(arm)} #{arm.name}" }.to_sentence %>
    children. The arms lost
    <%= reading.arms.map { |arm| "#{reading.extinct_count(arm)} #{arm.name}" }.to_sentence %>
    children to extinction.
  </p>
  <% if deep.any? %>
    <figure class="table-figure mt-4">
      <figcaption class="table-caption text-sm text-muted" id="meta-stack-finding-deep-children">
        The deep children, read from their stored samples at render time: the first epoch each
        deep rung held a tenth of the world under the persistence rule.
      </figcaption>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="meta-stack-finding-deep-children">
        <table class="data-table" aria-labelledby="meta-stack-finding-deep-children">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Child</th>
              <th>Parent</th>
              <th class="numeric">Seed</th>
              <% Lab::LogicReading::DEEP_TASKS.each do |task| %>
                <th class="numeric">First <%= task.upcase %></th>
              <% end %>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% deep.each do |child| %>
              <tr>
                <td><%= link_to "run #{child.run_id}", run_path(child.run_id) %></td>
                <td><%= link_to "run #{child.parent_id}", run_path(child.parent_id) %></td>
                <td class="numeric"><%= child.seed %></td>
                <% Lab::LogicReading::DEEP_TASKS.each do |task| %>
                  <% epoch = child.logic.first_epochs[task] %>
                  <td class="numeric"><%= epoch ? number_with_delimiter(epoch, delimiter: " ") : "—" %></td>
                <% end %>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </figure>
  <% end %>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    Every count above is read from the two sweeps' stored samples at render time, through the
    same reading <%= link_to "the sweep page", experiment_path("meta-stack", anchor: "meta-stack-reading") %>
    draws.
  </p>

  <%= render "experiments/meta_stack_reading", reading: reading.report %>
<% else %>
  <p class="text-muted">
    No child of <%= link_to "the sweep", experiment_path("meta-stack") %> is in this database, so
    there is nothing to read here. This page reads the children at render time and states the
    claim from them.
  </p>
<% end %>

